   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# RQ2-bis on Test Case C (AP1D electrophysiology): error vs parameters vs cost at fixed BFGS budget\n",
    "\n",
    "> Note: this is the **Case C (AP1D, `src/TestCase_3.py`)** notebook of `RQ2-bis/protocol.md`, kept in the `RQ2-bis/ADR-1b/` folder by user choice (the folder name does not mean Case A).\n",
    "\n",
    "Same Monodomain + Aliev-Panfilov problem, data, splits, normalisation and loss (MSE + $4.7\\cdot 10^{-3}$ Tikhonov) as `RQ2/AP1D/TestCase_C.ipynb`, with two changes: the optimizer is **BFGS-only** (0 Adam + up to 1000 BFGS iterations, the same scipy BFGS as RQ2) and the sweeps are over the **size of the dynamics network** $\\mathcal{NN}_{\\mathrm{dyn}}$ (width/depth) and the **latent size** $n$. R2 (end-to-end) only. Two reconstructors are compared on the same cost axes:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Arm | Reconstructor | Trainable |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| L0 (Stages 0-3) | the original $17^5 \\to 1$ on $(\\mathbf{s},x)$, no $u$ input, no output transform (1480 params at $n=12$) | MLP |\n",
    "| L2 (Stage 7) | $\\bar y+\\sum_{k=1}^{K}(W\\mathbf{s}+\\mathbf{b})_k\\varphi_k$ on the Legendre basis, strictly linear | $W,\\mathbf{b}$ |\n",
    "\n",
    "| Item | Value |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Canonical $\\mathcal{NN}_{\\mathrm{dyn}}$ | 8-$d_s$ base on $(\\mathbf{s},\\mathbf{u})$ with equilibrium subtraction **re-evaluated at every call** (as in the original script), $w^*=8$, $L^*=1$ hidden layer, $n^*=12$ (228 params) |\n",
    "| Width sweep (Stage 1) | $w \\in \\{2,4,8,16,32\\}$ = $\\{w^*/4,w^*/2,w^*,2w^*,4w^*\\}$, $L=L^*$, $n=n^*$ |\n",
    "| Depth sweep (Stage 1) | $L \\in \\{1,2,3\\}$ hidden layers at $w=w^*$, $n=n^*$ (only $L=2,3$ add runs) |\n",
    "| Latent sweep L0 (Stage 2) | $n \\in \\{3,6,12,24\\}$ at the canonical dynamics size |\n",
    "| Linear arm (Stage 7) | $K=65$ Legendre modes: $n$ sweep $\\{3,6,12,24\\}$ at canonical dynamics; width sweep and $K \\in \\{5,17,33,65\\}$ sweep at $n=12$ |\n",
    "| Iteration budget | 0 Adam + 1000 BFGS max (hard cap); checkpoints at $\\{25,50,100,200,500,1000\\}$ BFGS iterations (Stage 3, no extra runs) |\n",
    "| Seeds | $\\{0,1,2\\}$, seed 0 is the original script seed; median + min-max reported |\n",
    "\n",
    "Stages: **0** feasibility gate (canonical x 3 seeds) · **1** dynamics capacity · **2** latent dimension · **3** iteration surface from checkpoints · **5** thread scaling + serial timing (Pass T) · **7** linear reconstructor arm. **Stage 4 (long anchor to 5000) is dropped**: it exceeds the 1000-iteration cap. Stage 6 is out.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cost axes.** `n_fev` counts joint function/gradient evaluations (line-search steps included). Because L0 and L2 do very different work per evaluation, runs also store `flops_per_eval`, a formula count of multiply-adds of one loss+gradient evaluation on the training set ($3\\times$ forward, activations ignored; see `flops_per_eval`), and `flops_total` $=$ `flops_per_eval` $\\times$ `n_fev`. Stage 5 measures seconds per evaluation of every stored configuration (Pass T), so training time $\\approx$ `n_fev` $\\times$ `s_per_eval`, and checks the formula against it. Wall-times measured inside a sweep (Pass A) exclude tracing and checkpoint evaluation but were taken on a shared machine: orientation only.\n",
    "\n",
    "Deviations from `protocol.md` are listed in its Section 4/12: optimizer is scipy **BFGS** (RQ2's, kept unchanged except an observation hook and an evaluation counter), not L-BFGS; no `latents/` (R2 only); RQ2-style per-folder layout; no FLOP profiler (formula + measured time instead). $K_{\\mathrm{ref}}=33$ Legendre modes is the fixed floor of the efficiency ratio for L0 (L2 uses its own $K$).\n",
    "\n",
    "## How to use\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Run **Setup**, **Experiment configuration** and **Helpers** (cheap; after a restart run only these, then any analysis cell).\n",
    "2. Run the stage sections in order. Each trains its missing runs, then draws its plots. Re-running only re-draws.\n",
    "3. Stage 5 starts fresh processes (`timing_worker.py`); run it alone on a quiet machine. The **final comparison** only reads results.\n",
    "\n",
    "Budget: 30 L0 runs (10 configs) + 33 L2 runs (11 configs). Pilot rate (RQ2, 200+500): ~130-160 s/run; at 0+1000 expect ~2.5-3.5 h serial for L0 (L2 should be cheaper per evaluation: measured in Stage 5). A sweep cell skips runs already in `runs.csv`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything is stored in `results/`: `runs.csv` (one row per run), `predictions.csv` (one row per test sample), `curves.csv` (one row per iteration checkpoint), `weights/` (rebuild any run via `predict_test`), `timing.csv` + `hardware.json` (Stage 5), `meta.json` (versions, git hash, training settings).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reproducibility.** The train/valid subsampling is fixed across seeds (`np.random.seed(0)` once, original order). Every run calls `set_seed(seed)` before creating networks; TensorFlow is deterministic, CPU, float64."
   ]
  },
  {
