    "### Metrics (protocol Sec. 8) and result tables\n",
    "\n",
    "Every run appends one row to `runs.csv` (keyed by `variant, K, width, depth, d_s, seed`), one row per test sample to `predictions.csv`, and one row per iteration checkpoint to `curves.csv`:\n",
    "\n",
    "| file | columns |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `runs.csv` | `dyn_params`, `rec_params`, `p_total` (counted), `flops_per_eval`, `flops_total`, `n_fev`, `n_iters`, `nrmse_{train,valid,test}`, `one_minus_rho_{train,valid,test}`, `eps_total_test`, `eps_proj_test`, `eff_ratio_test`, `act_mae_test`, `act_miss_test`, `trace_time_s`, `train_time_s`, `infer_time_s`, `failed` |\n",
    "| `curves.csv` | `iter` (BFGS iterations completed), `n_fev`, `time_s`, `loss_train`, `loss_valid`, `nrmse_valid`, `nrmse_test` |\n",
    "\n",
    "- **NRMSE** / **Pearson dissimilarity** are those of the original script (denormalized fields). Train/valid on the 20 sampled points, test on the full grid.\n",
    "- **Efficiency ratio**: $\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{proj}}$ is the mean-subtracted Legendre residual floor with $K_{\\mathrm{ref}}=33$ modes for L0 and with the run's own $K$ for L2 (it only diagnoses whether the dynamics are the bottleneck).\n",
    "- **Case-C extras**: `act_mae` = mean absolute error (ms) of the activation time (first $t$ with $u \\ge 0.5$) over the grid points where **both** the FOM and the prediction activate; `act_miss` = fraction of the points where the FOM activates but the prediction never does (a model that fails to activate would otherwise look good on `act_mae`).\n",
    "- **Cost**: counted parameters, `n_fev`, completed BFGS iterations `n_iters` (a warning is printed if scipy stops before the cap), formula operations, wall-times. `trace_time_s` is the tf.function tracing; `train_time_s` is the BFGS loop only, **without the checkpoint evaluations** (a checkpoint predicts the whole test set).\n",
    "- A run with non-finite predictions is stored with `failed = True` and NaN metrics: it is counted, never silently dropped (statistics skip it)."
   ]
