    "### Runs\n",
    "\n",
    "`setup_run` rebuilds every object of a run from its seed (dynamics base first, then the reconstructor, as in the original script). `run_one` trains it (0 Adam + up to 1000 BFGS, per-epoch log silenced) and logs validation/test NRMSE at `CHECKPOINTS` from the single run into `curves.csv` (Stage 3). The hook is an observation only, and the time it takes is **subtracted** from the training time. A run whose predictions are not finite is stored as `failed` instead of crashing the sweep. `sweep` runs the missing `(seed, configuration)` pairs, so an interrupted sweep resumes. `trained_nets` rebuilds a stored run from its weights (predictions, rank analysis, timing). `time_eval` is the Pass-T unit of cost: seconds per joint function/gradient evaluation on a stored run (it is also what `timing_worker.py` calls in a fresh process)."
   ]
